module

public import LeanCategories.Algebra.KostantPBWData

/-!
# Kostant's integral form: definition-level data

Humphreys FC14-C07-U026 defines `U(L)_ℤ` to be the unital subring of
the universal enveloping algebra generated by all divided powers
`x_α^n / n!` of the chosen Chevalley root vectors.

TauCeti's Kostant development supplies the same root-generator/closure
construction, together with a stronger presentation that also includes
Cartan binomial generators.  Sweep III records only Humphreys' root-only
definition here.  The theorem identifying this subring with the free
`ℤ`-module on the triangular `f_A h_B e_C` elements, and hence showing
that the Cartan binomials belong to it, is FC14-C07-U027 result content.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

namespace LeanCategories.Algebra

universe u v w

variable (K : Type u) (L : Type v)
variable [Field K] [CharZero K] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L]

/-- The source generator set
`{x_α^n / n! | α ∈ Φ, n ≥ 0}` inside `U(L)`. -/
def kostantRootDividedPowerGenerators {Phi : Type w} (x : Phi → L) :
    Set (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) :=
  Set.range fun p : Phi × ℕ => ueaDividedPower K L (x p.1) p.2

/-- Humphreys' Kostant integral form `U(L)_ℤ`: the smallest unital
subring of `U(L)` containing every divided power of every supplied
Chevalley root vector.

No basis theorem or Cartan-binomial membership is built into this
definition. -/
def kostantIntegralFormData {Phi : Type w} (x : Phi → L) :
    Subring (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) :=
  Subring.closure (kostantRootDividedPowerGenerators K L x)

end LeanCategories.Algebra
